### Quick checklist for a clean Cursor-based workflow

- [ ] Remove `lovable-tagger` import and plugin usage from `vite.config.ts`.
- [ ] Remove `lovable-tagger` from `devDependencies` in `package.json` and re-run `npm install`.
- [ ] Update `index.html` title, meta description, author, and social preview tags to reflect your personal portfolio.
- [ ] Rewrite `README.md` to describe the project in neutral terms (no Lovable references).
- [ ] Confirm `npm run dev` works and serves the app at `http://localhost:8080`.
- [ ] Optionally run `npm run build` and `npm run preview` to confirm production builds work as expected.

Once the above are done, this project is fully “de-Lovable’d” and behaves exactly like a standard Vite + React + TypeScript app managed directly in Cursor.
